## Hypothesis A — Complexity identity

[
D_i
===

\Sigma_i^{\ast},
]

where (\Sigma_i^{\ast}) is the relevant conjunction of:

* causal emergence;
* predictive closure;
* semantic information;
* temporal integration.

The challenge is to identify necessary and sufficient conditions.

## Hypothesis B — Complexity plus fundamental bridge

[
\Sigma_i^{\ast}
\overset{B}{\longrightarrow}
D_i.
]

Here (B) is a fundamental psychophysical law.

The structure determines the field, but does not constitute it by conceptual necessity.

## Hypothesis C — Complexity as participation map

[
D_i
===

\pi_{\Sigma_i^{\ast}}(M_0).
]

The complex system individuates and structures a more fundamental capacity for manifestation.

